{{!< default}}

<!-- Hero Section: Story Title and Group Photo -->
<section class="heros-section redesigneds-hero">
  <div class="heros-wrapper">
    <div class="heros-content">
      <h1 class="heros-title">How Filter Coffee, FOSS, and a Few Restless Minds Started a Movement.</h1>
      <p class="heros-intro">Discover the story behind OASIS – where passion for open-source meets the drive to transform the social sector.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="heros-main">
      <div class="heros-left">
        <div class="heros-image">
          <img src="{{asset 'images/team.webp'}}" alt="Group photo at OASIS event" class="full-width-imgs" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <h2 class="heros-subtitle">Being long-time FOSS advocates, we knew high-quality, low-cost open tech was everywhere, so the real "wait a minute…" moment was this:</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gaps-section redesigneds-gap premium-timeline">
  <div class="containers">
    <header class="gaps-header">
      <h2 class="sections-title">Why does the social sector still struggle with tech?</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="timeline-static-wrapper">
      <div class="timeline-connector"></div>
      <div class="timeline-static-track">
        <div class="static-card">
          <div class="card-dot"></div>
          <div class="card-content">
            <p>When the world's biggest servers hum on open-source code, it's ironic that nonprofits still run on Google Sheets.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="static-card">
          <div class="card-dot"></div>
          <div class="card-content">
            <p><strong>FOSS United, Tech4Good Community, Reap Benefit, Aikyam, & TinkerHub</strong> began experimenting—from tech volunteering to open-source pilots for NGOs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="static-card">
          <div class="card-dot"></div>
          <div class="card-content">
            <p>Scattered efforts and caffeine-fueled chats at the <strong>JP Nagar office, </strong>drew a circle of tinkerers united by one goal: building a real tech muscle.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="static-card">
          <div class="card-dot"></div>
          <div class="card-content">
            <p>Over endless filter coffees, we realised fixes couldn't be quick hacks. The sector needed a shift: turning digital potential from <strong>"good-to-have"</strong> into an <strong>essential</strong>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="static-card final-destination">
          <div class="card-dot"></div>
          <div class="card-content oasis-theme">
            <span class="step-label text-white">2023 - 2024</span>
            <h3>OASIS</h3>
            <p>From the first Summit at BIC to a full-time team supported by Samagata. A movement proving open tech drives open change.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

